{"info": {"author": null, "author_email": "Dmitry Dygalo <dmitry@dygalo.dev>", "bugtrack_url": null, "classifiers": ["Development Status :: 5 - Production/Stable", "Environment :: Console", "Environment :: Web Environment", "Framework :: Django", "Framework :: Django :: 5.2", "Framework :: Django :: 6.0", "Framework :: Django :: 6.1", "Framework :: Pytest", "Intended Audience :: Developers", "Operating System :: OS Independent", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3 :: Only", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.11", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.12", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.13", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.14", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.15", "Programming Language :: Python :: Implementation :: CPython", "Programming Language :: Python :: Implementation :: PyPy", "Topic :: Communications :: Email", "Topic :: Software Development :: Libraries :: Python Modules", "Typing :: Typed"], "description": "# Postmarker\n\n[![Build](https://github.com/Stranger6667/postmarker/actions/workflows/build.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/Stranger6667/postmarker/actions/workflows/build.yml) [![Coverage](https://codecov.io/gh/Stranger6667/postmarker/branch/master/graph/badge.svg)](https://codecov.io/gh/Stranger6667/postmarker) [![Version](https://img.shields.io/pypi/v/postmarker.svg)](https://pypi.org/project/postmarker/) [![Python versions](https://img.shields.io/pypi/pyversions/postmarker.svg)](https://pypi.org/project/postmarker/) [![Docs](https://readthedocs.org/projects/postmarker/badge/?version=stable)](https://postmarker.readthedocs.io/en/stable/) [![License](https://img.shields.io/pypi/l/postmarker.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)\n\nPython client for the [Postmark](https://postmarkapp.com) email API.\n\nPostmarker covers Postmark's API beyond sending: templates, bounces, suppressions, message streams, stats, servers and domains.\nIt also ships a Django email backend, Postmark webhook wrappers and a pytest fixture for your tests.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Postmarker keeps Postmark's field names: `From`, `HtmlBody`, `TemplateModel`, `MessageStream`.\n> Copy any field from the [Postmark API docs](https://postmarkapp.com/developer) and pass it as is. There are no snake_case aliases.\n\n## Installation\n\n```\nuv pip install postmarker\n```\n\nTo inline `<style>` CSS into HTML emails, install the `css-inline` extra and create the client with `inline_css=True`:\n\n```\nuv pip install 'postmarker[css-inline]'\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n```python\nfrom postmarker.core import PostmarkClient\n\npostmark = PostmarkClient(server_token=\"POSTMARK_API_TEST\")\npostmark.emails.send(\n    From=\"sender@example.com\",\n    To=\"receiver@example.com\",\n    Subject=\"Postmark test\",\n    HtmlBody=\"<strong>Hello</strong> dear Postmark user.\",\n)\n# {\"ErrorCode\": 0, \"Message\": \"Test job accepted\", \"MessageID\": \"...\", ...}\n```\n\nWith the `POSTMARK_API_TEST` token, Postmark validates the request without delivering it.\nTo send real emails, use the server token from your server's API Tokens tab in Postmark.\n`From` must be a confirmed sender signature or an address on a verified domain.\n\nSend with a template:\n\n```python\npostmark.emails.send_with_template(\n    TemplateAlias=\"welcome\",\n    TemplateModel={\"name\": \"Jane\"},\n    From=\"sender@example.com\",\n    To=\"receiver@example.com\",\n)\n```\n\nSend a batch. Postmarker splits it into requests of 500 messages, Postmark's limit:\n\n```python\nmessages = [\n    {\"From\": \"sender@example.com\", \"To\": to, \"Subject\": \"Hi\", \"TextBody\": \"Hello\"}\n    for to in (\"first@example.com\", \"second@example.com\")\n]\nresponses = postmark.emails.send_batch(*messages)\n# Postmark accepts or rejects each message separately\nfailed = [response for response in responses if response[\"ErrorCode\"] != 0]\n```\n\nAdd headers and attachments:\n\n```python\nemail = postmark.emails.Email(\n    From=\"sender@example.com\",\n    To=\"receiver@example.com\",\n    Subject=\"Report\",\n    TextBody=\"See the attached report.\",\n)\nemail[\"X-Accept-Language\"] = \"en-us, en\"\nemail.attach(\"/home/user/report.pdf\")\nemail.attach_binary(content=b\"content\", filename=\"readme.txt\")\nemail.send()\n```\n\nA rejected request raises `ClientError` with Postmark's [error code](https://postmarkapp.com/developer/api/overview#error-codes):\n\n```python\nfrom postmarker.exceptions import ClientError\n\ntry:\n    postmark.emails.send(\n        From=\"sender@example.com\",\n        To=\"receiver@example.com\",\n        TextBody=\"Hello\",\n    )\nexcept ClientError as exc:\n    print(exc.error_code)  # For example, 406 for an inactive recipient\n```\n\n## Async\n\n`AsyncPostmarkClient` has the same API, with every method that makes a request as a coroutine.\nInstall the `async` extra:\n\n```\nuv pip install 'postmarker[async]'\n```\n\n```python\nfrom postmarker.core import AsyncPostmarkClient\n\nasync with AsyncPostmarkClient(server_token=\"POSTMARK_API_TEST\") as postmark:\n    await postmark.emails.send(\n        From=\"sender@example.com\",\n        To=\"receiver@example.com\",\n        TextBody=\"Hello\",\n    )\n```\n\nSee the [async guide](https://postmarker.readthedocs.io/en/stable/async/) for properties, fixtures and differences.\n\n## Django\n\nDjango 6.1+:\n\n```python\nMAILERS = {\n    \"default\": {\n        \"BACKEND\": \"postmarker.django.EmailBackend\",\n        \"OPTIONS\": {\"token\": \"<YOUR POSTMARK SERVER TOKEN>\"},\n    },\n}\n```\n\nDjango 5.2 and 6.0:\n\n```python\nEMAIL_BACKEND = \"postmarker.django.EmailBackend\"\nPOSTMARK = {\"TOKEN\": \"<YOUR POSTMARK SERVER TOKEN>\"}\n```\n\nDjango then sends `send_mail`, `EmailMessage` and emails from third-party apps through Postmark.\nThe [Django guide](https://postmarker.readthedocs.io/en/stable/django/) covers tags, metadata, message streams and signals.\n\n## Testing\n\nPostmarker ships a `postmark_request` pytest fixture.\nIt mocks requests to Postmark and records what your code sent, through `PostmarkClient` or the Django backend:\n\n```python\ndef test_welcome_email(postmark_request):\n    send_welcome_email(\"jane@example.com\")  # Your code that sends an email\n    assert postmark_request.call_args.kwargs[\"json\"][\"To\"] == \"jane@example.com\"\n```\n\n## Features\n\n- Server APIs: Emails, Templates with layouts, Bounces, Messages (inbound, outbound, opens and clicks), Message Streams, Suppressions, Server, Stats and Triggers.\n- Account APIs: Domains, Sender signatures, Servers and pushing templates between servers.\n- Status and Spam check APIs.\n- Webhook wrappers: Inbound, Delivery, Open, Click, Bounce, Spam complaint and Subscription change.\n- Sending `email.message.Message` instances.\n- CSS inlining via [css-inline](https://github.com/Stranger6667/css-inline).\n- Async client (`AsyncPostmarkClient`) via the `async` extra.\n- Django email backend and Tornado helper.\n- Type annotations, with a `py.typed` marker.\n\n## Documentation\n\n<https://postmarker.readthedocs.io/en/stable/>\n\n## Python support\n\nPostmarker supports CPython 3.11 to 3.15 and PyPy 3.11. The Django email backend supports Django 5.2, 6.0 and 6.1.\n", "description_content_type": "text/markdown", "docs_url": null, "download_url": null, "downloads": {"last_day": -1, "last_month": -1, "last_week": -1}, "dynamic": null, "home_page": null, "keywords": "api, client, django, email, email backend, postmark, postmarkapp, transactional email", "license": null, "license_expression": "MIT", "license_files": ["LICENSE"], "maintainer": null, "maintainer_email": "Dmitry Dygalo <dmitry@dygalo.dev>", "name": "postmarker", "package_url": "https://pypi.org/project/postmarker/", "platform": null, "project_url": "https://pypi.org/project/postmarker/", "project_urls": {"Bug Tracker": "https://github.com/Stranger6667/postmarker/issues", "Changelog": "https://github.com/Stranger6667/postmarker/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md", "Documentation": "https://postmarker.readthedocs.io/en/stable/", "Funding": "https://github.com/sponsors/Stranger6667", "Source Code": "https://github.com/Stranger6667/postmarker"}, "provides_extra": ["async", "css-inline", "docs", "tests"], "release_url": "https://pypi.org/project/postmarker/3.0/", "requires_dist": ["requests>=2.20.0", "httpx2>=2.16; extra == \"async\"", "css-inline>=0.24; extra == \"css-inline\"", "mkdocstrings[python]; extra == \"docs\"", "pymdown-extensions; extra == \"docs\"", "ruff; extra == \"docs\"", "zensical<0.2,>=0.1.1; extra == \"docs\"", "coverage[toml]>=7.2; extra == \"tests\"", "css-inline>=0.24; extra == \"tests\"", "httpx2>=2.16; extra == \"tests\"", "pytest-django; extra == \"tests\"", "pytest-recording>=0.14; extra == \"tests\"", "pytest>=8; extra == \"tests\"", "tornado; extra == \"tests\""], "requires_python": ">=3.11", "summary": "Python client library for Postmark API", "version": "3.0", "yanked": false, "yanked_reason": null}, "release_dates": {"0.0.1": "2016-10-04T14:06:55.424632Z", "0.1.0": "2016-10-05T09:33:22.716139Z", "0.1.1": "2016-10-05T10:15:03.652307Z", "0.10.0": "2017-03-30T14:22:47.645848Z", "0.10.1": "2017-04-03T18:45:50.671955Z", "0.11.0": "2017-05-02T09:31:16.080234Z", "0.11.1": "2017-05-10T13:55:48.146568Z", "0.11.2": "2017-05-14T07:26:52.336168Z", "0.11.3": "2017-11-08T12:19:09.229853Z", "0.12.0": "2018-06-12T07:56:47.855285Z", "0.12.1": "2018-11-05T18:26:48.503004Z", "0.12.2": "2018-11-05T18:56:21.269067Z", "0.13.0": "2018-11-25T13:28:20.551171Z", "0.13.1": "2019-11-15T15:44:23.947706Z", "0.14.0": "2020-02-10T10:54:36.343448Z", "0.14.1": "2020-03-31T14:47:02.797892Z", "0.15.0": "2020-08-30T13:46:59.606117Z", "0.16.0": "2020-11-10T16:01:51.645848Z", "0.17.0": "2020-12-22T13:17:40.185711Z", "0.17.1": "2021-03-02T15:02:39.641770Z", "0.18.0": "2021-05-11T06:19:05.588276Z", "0.18.1": "2021-05-13T14:47:43.434505Z", "0.18.2": "2021-06-03T09:36:14.937918Z", "0.2.0": "2016-10-07T07:25:10.850556Z", "0.3.0": "2016-10-07T14:51:51.726043Z", "0.3.1": "2016-10-08T09:56:42.5